      "id": 1,
      "text": "Fisher was founded in 1875, making it one of Illinois' older villages.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fisher%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "South of Fisher on Route 47 stands Shiloh Methodist Church, one of the county’s oldest churches.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.news-gazette.com/history-of-fisher/collection_8c518974-814b-5551-aec9-436a87fe07b4.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Fisher Community Fair and Horse Show, first held in 1941, draws thousands each July for a weeklong celebration.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.champaigncounty.org/fisher/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every July, the Lucky Foot Festival and Ranae Helpingstine Memorial Car Show bring music, cars, and family activities to Fisher.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.champaigncounty.org/fisher/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The first building for the Fisher National Bank still stands as a reminder of the town’s early financial history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.news-gazette.com/history-of-fisher/collection_8c518974-814b-5551-aec9-436a87fe07b4.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The original Fisher Public School was torn down in 1914, a loss remembered by longtime residents.",
